- 11 of Caravaca Puchades's lines were committed by Troy Goode, and 6 of LuisEGR's were committed by Wilson. The tool credits them to the original authors.

## Ownership risk

- The bus factor is 1: Goode alone holds over half the lines.
- Only 1 of 18 authors has committed in the last 365 days. That is Goode, and they hold 67.3% of the lines. The other 32.7% belongs to people with no commit in that time.
- Wilson's 9.3% is the largest share held by someone who is no longer active.

This measures how many lines survived, not code quality, review work, or design decisions made elsewhere. Commit `fcd2b56` ("switch to ESLint; clean up", Goode, 5 surviving lines) may be a mechanical rewrite. I didn't set it aside, so those 5 lines are credited to Goode.

